<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Mansur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1393</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Shah Mansur Muzaffari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Mansur was a prince of the Muzaffarid dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the 14th century, and its last effective ruler, seizing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> in 1387. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> invaded again, he defied him and in 1393 led a desperate charge against Timur's army near Shiraz, where he was killed. Timur then executed the remaining Muzaffarid princes and annexed their lands.</p></div>
